{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.QBetaRadiusOfConvergenceGate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.QBetaRadiusOfConvergenceGate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.gate_satisfied_at_exact_match","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.gate_satisfied_at_exact_match","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate.lean#L129-L138","doc":"**Composition with the fibre-level tolerance**: the gate's\noperational form allows a small tolerance (`1e-6` per PR #1727's\nfibre-level swing bound). This lemma states that if a candidate\nmatches `u_substrate` exactly, the gate is satisfied (the\nconverse / approximate form is the operational version used by\nthe sympy probe). Pure ring identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.radius_of_convergence_gate_reject","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.radius_of_convergence_gate_reject","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate.lean#L107-L127","doc":"**The gate theorem (refute direction): the rejection lemma.**\n\nIf a candidate predicts a pole location `u_0` and `u_0 ≠ u_substrate`,\nthen the `RadiusOfConvergenceGateClass` cannot be instantiated for\nthat candidate — i.e., the candidate is structurally REFUTED.\n\nThis is the contrapositive of the forward gate: in the gate's\noperational use, a probe computes the candidate's pole location,\ncompares against `u_substrate`, and rejects on mismatch beyond the\n1 ppm fibre-level tolerance.  The Lean statement here makes that\nrejection an instantiability obstruction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.qbeta_g_simple_pole_at_u_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.qbeta_g_simple_pole_at_u_substrate","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate.lean#L94-L105","doc":"**The gate theorem (forward direction): under the class, the\ncandidate's pole location is u_substrate.**\n\nTrivial restatement of the class field — the value of formalising\nis composition with downstream checks (e.g. cross-anchor swing\nbounds, fibre-level analyticity).  Mirrors the\n`q_beta_n3_structural_form` pattern from `QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate","label":"conj:q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.RadiusOfConvergenceGateClass.pole_location_is_u_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.RadiusOfConvergenceGateClass.pole_location_is_u_substrate","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate.lean#L91-L91","doc":"Structural identity: the candidate's pole location equals\n`u_substrate`. A candidate violating this fails the gate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.RadiusOfConvergenceGateClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.RadiusOfConvergenceGateClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.RadiusOfConvergenceGateClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.RadiusOfConvergenceGateClass","kind":"class","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate.lean#L77-L92","doc":"**Radius-of-convergence gate class (§3b-cond, mirrors\n`QbetaC3StructuralFormClass`).**\n\nAxiomatises the framework's structural prediction (PR #1727) that\nthe true Q_β ladder coefficients satisfy the asymptotic ratio\ntest `c_{k+1} / c_k → 1/u_substrate` (the simple-pole signature\nat `u = u_substrate`). The class is purely conditional (no\ninstance); production wires only the verified PR #1727 asymptotic\nconstants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.u_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.u_substrate","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate.lean#L68-L75","doc":"**The established u_substrate value (PR #1727 cross-anchor).**\n\nNumerical constant from the canonical SDP extraction at\nproton-pinned q_0, verified at 210 ppb fibre-level tolerance\nagainst q_muon (PR #1727 / `qbeta_singularity_cross_anchor_probe.py`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.qBetaCandidatePoleLocation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.qBetaCandidatePoleLocation","kind":"axiom","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate.lean#L59-L66","doc":"**Abstract candidate pole location.**\n\nThe candidate's `g(u) = Σ c_k u^k` has nearest pole at this `u`\nvalue. The framework's prediction (PR #1727) is that for the TRUE\nQ_β kernel, this equals `u_substrate ≈ 0.00852`. A candidate\nfailing to predict this location is REFUTED. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.qBetaLadderCoefficients","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RadiusOfConvergenceGate.qBetaLadderCoefficients","kind":"axiom","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-radius-of-convergence-gate.lean#L48-L57","doc":"**Abstract candidate ladder coefficient sequence.**\n\nFollowing the §3b-cond pattern (mirrors `qBetaC3Categorical` in\n`QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean`), we declare an abstract\nsequence `c_k : ℕ → R` representing the ladder coefficients\ngenerated by some candidate Habiro element F(q). Its closed form\nis the open research target; the radius-of-convergence gate\noperates on its asymptotic ratio. ","signatureChunk":0}]}